  "description": "The Fuji Team is the coolest\nbike anywhere near its price. The 18-lb Team has been so successful, Fuji's\nproduct people thought an upgraded Team might be\nin order.\n\nA Team SL is a Team, except for: a Ritchey integrated headset, WCS stem,\nLogic Pro Road handlebars; American Classic hubs and Ritchey Pro Road\nrims; FSA carbon/aluminum cranks and carbon seatpost.\n\nI have a Fuji Team, and I love it. It's light and smooth. It makes me\nfeel fast as Gord Fraser sprinting for city limit signs. A Team SL might\nbe better yet, but Fuji would want me to give up my Team. Have to sedate\nme.\nMy Team has been an eye-opener for me. Aluminum's reputed harsh ride is\nnowhere to be found. I believe that Fuji's product guys, old road-riders\nand industry veterans, made that harshness disappear, replaced it with\ncompliance. Look at both bikes and ride them if you can.\n\nThe SL upgrades are right there to see.\nIf you buy a Team SL, please: Don't be making riding life miserable for\nyour training buddies just because you can. There may be SLs in their\nfutures too...",
